# GlowUp repository: what is NOT kept in Git, and why.
# The repository holds the Unity app (GlowUp/) and the admin website (GlowUp-Admin_AI_Testing/).

# 1. The file that holds the AI key. It must never enter Git history, because history cannot be
#    cleaned afterwards. A fresh copy of this repository will not compile until this one file is
#    copied in by hand (its .meta file IS kept, so Unity recognises it again).
GlowUp/Assets/_Project/Scripts/Security/SecureProfileStore.cs

# 2. Folders and files Unity, Visual Studio and Gradle make again by themselves
GlowUp/Library/
GlowUp/Temp/
GlowUp/Logs/
GlowUp/obj/
GlowUp/Builds/
GlowUp/UserSettings/
GlowUp/MemoryCaptures/
GlowUp/Recordings/
GlowUp/.vs/
GlowUp/.gradle/
GlowUp/*_BurstDebugInformation_DoNotShip/
GlowUp/*_BackUpThisFolder_ButDontShipItWithYourGame/
GlowUp/*.csproj
GlowUp/*.sln
GlowUp/*.user
GlowUp/*.apk
GlowUp/*.aab

# 3. Downloads and hand-made backups (Git is the history from now on)
GlowUp/tesseract-unity-master/
GlowUp-Admin_Backup_*/
GlowUp-Unity_Backup_*/
GlowUp-Unity_Removed_*/
GlowUp-Data_Backup_*/
facebook-unity-sdk-*/
facebook-unity-sdk-*.unitypackage
facebook-unity-sdk-*.zip
GlowUp-Admin_AI_Testing/firebase_unity_sdk_*/

# 4. Website tool files
.vercel/
.env*
node_modules/
firestore-debug.log
*.bak

# 5. Windows and editor leftovers
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# 6. Local tool settings of this computer
.claude/
